# Residual RMSNorm pass 1: one block, no branches. The flops are exact;
# the loads and stores are masked (`@%p`), so the per-thread byte totals
# are upper bounds and AI(global) is a lower bound. Nothing unknown.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/gluon/rmsnorm_stats_kernel.sm_89.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK: kernel rmsnorm_stats_kernel
CHECK: $L__func_begin0  gluon_norm.py:37-64    1146  (end)
CHECK: block size: 128 threads, 4 warps (128x1x1 from .reqntid)
# The masks are constants: `mov.pred %p1, -1` keeps every lane, and the
# fourth vector of each row under `mov.pred %p2, 0` runs on no thread
# (ptxas emits no SASS for those lines, rmsnorm_stats_kernel.sm_89.ncu.json).
CHECK: warp: 16–17 sectors (ideal 16)
CHECK: global load 16 B on 0 threads in 0 warps (no thread)             warp: 0 sectors (ideal 0)
CHECK: flops = 534  (f32 534)
# Per thread the dead vectors count nothing either: 18 live 16 B and
# 2 live 4 B loads, plus the guarded `atom`'s 4 B.
CHECK: global bytes: load <= 300 B, store <= 108 B
CHECK: AI(global) >= 1.3186274509803921 flop/B
# Per CTA the live loads and stores measure 37888 B and 12320 B (the
# ncu record's LDG and STG executions); the `<=` and 4 B are the one
# guarded `atom`.
CHECK: totals per CTA [static]:
CHECK: global bytes: load <= 37892 B, store <= 12324 B
CHECK: unknowns: none
CHECK: coverage: instructions_classified 100.0% (1146/1146)
